The circularity now applies across an arbitrary tail, but the backend does not infer `not (e >= t) ⇔ e < t` from its integer constraints. I’m changing the source to test `<` directly: successful elements execute `continue`; the next statement returns `False`. This is equivalent Python, uses the contract’s literal predicate, and makes each invariant branch share the exact comparison atom with the summary.
