codex
The generic entry still forces the backend to discover the outer `ValSeq` constructor before it can use the loop theorem, and it keeps unrolling instead. I’m splitting only the whole-program entry into the native `.ValSeq` and `vCons(V,REST)` constructor cases. These two symbolic claims are exhaustive and still cover arbitrary finite heterogeneous numeric lists; no length bound is introduced.
