The final rule is blocked only on static-sort refinement: the target path knows `V` is numeric as a Boolean disjunction, but rule matching does not refine `V:Val`. I’m splitting the nonempty whole-program entry by its first element’s native sort (`Int`, `Bool`, `Float`). Those three cases plus empty are exhaustive; each tail remains an arbitrary symbolic numeric sequence, so this does not bound length or forbid mixed lists.
