codex
The final loop bridge works from an independently stated loop-head configuration, so the mismatch is caused by symbolic state normalization along the 33-step call prelude. I’m modularizing that prelude too: a bridge-free universal claim will prove exact module load, binding, frame creation, parameter binding, and `e = 0` up to (but not through) the loop head for arbitrary `ValSeq`. The target will then compose two exact, independently proved regions.
apply patch
